.page exit 1 leave the shell

# SYNOPSIS
*exit* [_STATUS_]

# DESCRIPTION
`exit` is a gapsh builtin: the shell stops with the exit status _STATUS_ (only the lowest eight bits count), or with the status of the last command if none is given. An `EXIT` trap, if one was set, runs first. In an interactive login shell the init process then starts a new one.

# SEE ALSO
return(1), trap(1)
